ost reporters Bob Woodward and Carl  Bernstein the talented cast is rounded  out by Diane Lane Tony Goldwyn Josh  Lucas and Michael C Hall literally right  before Erin Justin Long stars in  literally right before Aaron as Adam a  man still reeling from his recent  breakup when his ex-girlfriend calls to  let him know she's getting married Adam  agrees to go to the wedding and  predictably things quickly take a turn  for the worse  the Florida Project Shawn Baker's  tangerine follow up the Florida Project  has all the heart and beauty shown in  his early  your work albeit in a new setting this  time Baker investigates the lives of  those living in an extended stay motel  in Orlando focusing specifically on a  precocious six-year-old and the motels  owner Bobby played by Willem Dafoe Dafoe  is the grounding force of the trailer  but the child actors are given the  chance to shine as well already enjoying  rave reviews the florida project looks  like a beautiful touching exploration of  childhood we're all in cellblock 99 it's  Vince Vaughn like you've never seen him  before in the trailer for brawl and  cellblock 99 the latest action outing  from bone tomahawk director s Craig  dollar bond plays Bradley Thomas a  former boxer who resorts to drug running  in an effort to save his marriage after  losing his job as a mechanic things  quickly go wrong when a drug deal turns  deadly putting him behind bars goodbye  Christopher Robin the new trailer for  goodbye Christopher Robin stars domhnall  gleeson is a a Milne the author who  dreamed up we need the Pooh for his  young son Christopher Robin margot  robbie takes on the part of mills wife  Daphne in the film the trailer deals  heavily with Milne struggle with PTSD  but manages to balance drama humor and  heart in a way that will hopefully  translate into an effecting biopic  Batman vs two-face Adam West's final  performances Batman is teased in the  trailer for Batman vs two-face the  Batman legend reprised his role  alongside Burt Ward's Robin with the two  facing off against Harvey Dent voiced by  William Shatner in the sequel to 2016 s  Batman return of the Caped Crusader's  suburbicon directed by George Clooney  from a script co-written by the Coen  brothers suburbicon stars Matt Damon as  Gardner Lodge a man dealing with the  violent advances of a loan shark in his  small 1950s era American town Oscar  Isaac and Julianne Moore co-star and  with so many huge names attached it  looks like suburbicon is a town  audiences won't want to leave even if  the residents most definitely do last  flag flying break out the tissues before  you watch the trailer for Richard  Linklater's last flag flying  Steve Carell leads the drama D as  Richard doc said who recruits two of his  Vietnam buddies played by Brian Cranston  and Laurence Fishburne to help him bury  his son after he's killed in Iraq the  three leads have great chemistry and  they're growing bond helps anchor what  looks like an emotional cross-country  journey death wish Bruce Willis is out  for vigilante justice in the first  trailer for Eli  Deathwish a remake of the 1974 film of  the same name the movie follows Willis's  Paul Kersey a doctor who seeks revenge  after the violence in the streets of  Chicago spills into his own home while  remakes are old had at this point death  wish looks like it could be worth a trip  to the theater mollies game Jessica  Chastain stars as the smart  straight-talking Molly bloom in the  first trailer for Aaron Sorkin's  directorial debut Molly's game which  tells the true story of the  olympic-class skier who ran an exclusive  high-stakes poker game as the trailer  shows the movie follows Molly on her way  up in the poker world while also showing  her downfall  Chastain also has some impressive back  up in the movie with co-stars Idris Elba  and Michael Cera call me by your name  this Film Festival darling stars Armie  Hammer as Oliver an American professor  who travels to northern Italy in the  summer of 1983 while there he falls into  a relationship with a 17-year old  Italian boy with an early 100% on Rotten  Tomatoes call me by your name clearly  isn't a movie you want to miss super  troopers - it's been a long long time  coming but the first trailer for the  upcoming Super Troopers 2 is finally  here and it's awesome the sequel to the  cult cop comedy features the group of  Vermont State Troopers fighting with  Canada over the borderline setting up a  new highway patrol station right in the  conflicted zone considering the fact  that the original writers directors and  cast are all on board the sequel should  be well worth the wait  that's a funny mail is it Jim and I  explore the dark side of celebrity in  the trailer for Gemini the movie stars  Lola Kirk as Jill and assistant to a  Hollywood starlet named Heather played  by zoe kravitz when Heather is murdered  Jill learns she's a suspect causing her  to reevaluate her own views of  friendship truth and fame the trailer  hints that there could be more to  Heather's murder than meets the eye  raising a whole bunch of questions to be  answered in the film with already  stellar reviews from its film festival  premieres Gemini is a stylish murder  mystery we're looking forward to  figuring out the death of Stalin veep  creator Armando Iannucci is about to  satirize yet another country's  government judging by the first trailer  for the death of Stalin the movie shows  the mad rush for power after Stalin's  passing with Jeffrey Tambor Steve  Buscemi and Jason Isaacs playing  characters looking to take charge  I said no problem what I meant was no  problem it may not be a game of Thrones  level fight for power but we're  definitely on board to watch this not so  historical comedy thanks for watching  click the looper icon to subscribe to  our YouTube channel plus check out all  this cool stuff we know you'll love to  [Music]
 

